1
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:11,886
This is Milestone 2, the admission system,
shown on the live Portal.

2
00:00:11,958 --> 00:00:15,618
We will follow one person all the way in. She
applies, you question her, you approve her,

3
00:00:15,678 --> 00:00:19,338
you invite her, and she joins.

4
00:00:19,407 --> 00:00:22,447
This is the application form on the Institute
website. Anyone can reach it. No account, no

5
00:00:22,507 --> 00:00:25,547
password.

6
00:00:27,247 --> 00:00:31,687
There is room for three hundred characters in
the title, and the form says so, because

7
00:00:31,747 --> 00:00:36,187
people shorten their own titles when they
suspect a form will not accept them.

8
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:41,070
A professor of health systems applies.

9
00:00:44,834 --> 00:00:49,052
Her full title, a named chair with a
department and a second appointment, one

10
00:00:49,112 --> 00:00:53,330
hundred and eighty seven characters. Nothing
is abbreviated.

11
00:00:55,732 --> 00:00:59,578
And the confirmation. It does not promise a
date the Institute has not promised. It says a

12
00:00:59,638 --> 00:01:03,484
person will read it, which is true.

13
00:01:08,666 --> 00:01:11,206
Now your side of the Portal.

14
00:01:14,971 --> 00:01:17,856
Administrator accounts require a second
factor. This is enforced by the server, not

15
00:01:17,916 --> 00:01:20,801
the screen.

16
00:01:25,179 --> 00:01:29,619
The admission queue. Applications and
referrals in one list, oldest first, so nobody

17
00:01:29,679 --> 00:01:34,119
waits longest merely because they arrived by a
different route.

18
00:01:35,224 --> 00:01:37,764
Her case. Everything she wrote, in full.

19
00:01:38,742 --> 00:01:42,557
The long title wraps onto a second line. It is
never cut off with three dots. Whatever the

20
00:01:42,617 --> 00:01:46,432
Portal accepted, the Portal shows.

21
00:01:47,409 --> 00:01:51,937
Now the four actions. Two of them are
judgements, and two of them are not.

22
00:01:51,998 --> 00:01:57,022
Approve is final and permanent. Decline is
also final, and asks you to record why.

23
00:01:57,992 --> 00:02:01,311
Need more information is not a decision at
all. It is a question. The case stays open,

24
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:04,690
and you may ask again.

25
00:02:04,761 --> 00:02:09,201
That distinction matters. If a question were
recorded as a decision, someone you asked

26
00:02:09,261 --> 00:02:13,701
twice and then approved would appear to have
been decided upon three times.

27
00:02:14,683 --> 00:02:19,123
Set aside is a silent pause, for you. Nothing
is sent to anybody, and it stays here in the

28
00:02:19,183 --> 00:02:23,623
queue, because a case that vanishes when
paused is a case that gets forgotten.

29
00:02:27,058 --> 00:02:32,454
The case now reads awaiting information, and
it is still open. Nothing has been decided.

30
00:02:35,659 --> 00:02:38,854
Her reply is recorded, and the case returns to
you. Both the question and the answer stay in

31
00:02:38,914 --> 00:02:42,109
her history.

32
00:02:44,872 --> 00:02:48,966
Approved. Now notice what did not happen. She
has not been invited.

33
00:02:49,949 --> 00:02:54,389
Inviting is a separate act, offered only after
approval. Inviting somebody is a consequence

34
00:02:54,449 --> 00:02:58,889
of deciding about them, never another way of
deciding about them.

35
00:02:59,911 --> 00:03:03,385
The invitation form. Her name is the only
thing required.

36
00:03:04,404 --> 00:03:07,344
If you found somebody on LinkedIn and have no
email address for them, choose to send the

37
00:03:07,404 --> 00:03:10,344
link yourself. Most of the time you will not
have an address, and you should not have to

38
00:03:10,404 --> 00:03:13,344
invent one.

39
00:03:15,616 --> 00:03:20,888
A sentence in your own words, which appears in
the invitation exactly as you write it.

40
00:03:22,361 --> 00:03:24,901
And here is the link, shown once.

41
00:03:25,669 --> 00:03:29,174
Only a fingerprint of it is stored, so no page
anywhere can show it again. Not this page on a

42
00:03:29,234 --> 00:03:32,739
refresh, not anybody.

43
00:03:33,722 --> 00:03:37,537
If you lose it, one click issues a fresh link
and the old one stops working at that same

44
00:03:37,597 --> 00:03:41,412
moment. Losing it costs you a click.

45
00:04:18,169 --> 00:04:23,255
This is the concern you raised. Link scanners
open a link before any human sees it.

46
00:04:24,198 --> 00:04:26,738
Opened once.

47
00:04:27,719 --> 00:04:30,259
Twice.

48
00:04:31,299 --> 00:04:36,571
Three times, exactly as a scanner would. And
the invitation is still perfectly usable.

49
00:04:36,638 --> 00:04:41,078
It is only spent when somebody actually
finishes registering, so a scanner can never

50
00:04:41,138 --> 00:04:45,578
burn an invitation before it reaches the
person it was meant for.

51
00:04:46,563 --> 00:04:49,107
And there is your sentence, in your words.

52
00:04:50,085 --> 00:04:54,525
She confirms her own details rather than being
stuck with what you typed. You are the

53
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:59,025
authority on who is admitted. She is the
authority on the facts of her own life.

54
00:04:59,193 --> 00:05:02,133
This field is how she tells the Portal what to
call her. If it is blank we use her first

55
00:05:02,193 --> 00:05:05,133
name, and if we do not confidently know a name
we greet her without one, rather than send

56
00:05:05,193 --> 00:05:08,133
Hello comma.

57
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:13,571
Consent is recorded at this moment, against
the privacy notice in force.

58
00:05:17,489 --> 00:05:20,029
She is now an admitted collaborator.

59
00:05:21,016 --> 00:05:23,556
Collaborators can recommend people too.

60
00:05:25,605 --> 00:05:28,521
And here is the relationship question you
added.

61
00:05:29,314 --> 00:05:33,687
Not Mentor and Mentee, which cannot say who
mentored whom, but I mentored them, and They

62
00:05:33,747 --> 00:05:38,120
mentored me. The same question, without the
ambiguity.

63
00:05:39,332 --> 00:05:43,772
The referrer is told, right here, that these
answers are seen by the Institute alone. They

64
00:05:43,832 --> 00:05:48,272
never reach the person being recommended, and
never appear on a profile.

65
00:05:51,299 --> 00:05:56,323
Nothing has been sent to Kestutis. He may not
know he has been recommended at all.

66
00:06:10,785 --> 00:06:15,003
On your side, the referral arrives marked seen
by the Institute only.

67
00:06:15,073 --> 00:06:19,513
If you need to understand something before
deciding, the Portal asks the referrer, never

68
00:06:19,573 --> 00:06:24,013
him. The Institute does not contact a referred
professional until you have approved them.

69
00:06:27,087 --> 00:06:30,220
And here is her whole story in one place.
Applied, questioned, answered, approved,

70
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:33,413
invited, registered.

71
00:06:33,481 --> 00:06:37,761
This is assembled from the records themselves
rather than kept as a separate log, so it

72
00:06:37,821 --> 00:06:42,101
cannot quietly disagree with what actually
happened.

73
00:06:43,855 --> 00:06:48,445
The invitation link again, now that it has
been used. Single use, enforced.

74
00:06:49,406 --> 00:06:52,725
And a link that expired, or was withdrawn, or
never existed at all, is met with this. Never

75
00:06:52,785 --> 00:06:56,104
an error message.

76
00:06:56,168 --> 00:07:00,608
Arriving at a lapsed link is not a mistake the
visitor made. A wrong guess sees exactly these

77
00:07:00,668 --> 00:07:05,108
same words, so nothing tells anybody whether
they found something real.
